# RUN: %python -c "import struct; open(r'%t.sys', 'wb').write(struct.pack('<IHHH8s', 0xffffffff, 0x8000, 18, 19, b'WHPTEST ') + bytes([0xcb, 0xcb]))"
# RUN: llvm-readobj --dos-device-header %t.sys | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DRIVER
# RUN: not llvm-readobj --dos-device-header %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INVALID
#
# DRIVER: Format: DOSDevice
# DRIVER: DOSDeviceHeader {
# DRIVER: NextDevice: 0xFFFFFFFF
# DRIVER: Attributes: 0x8000
# DRIVER: DeviceType: Character
# DRIVER: StrategyOffset: 0x12
# DRIVER: InterruptOffset: 0x13
# DRIVER: DeviceName: WHPTEST
# INVALID: invalid initial DOS device header link
